---
/**
 * What players ask before they play: how to get it running, levels in an open world, how it battles,
 * trading and saves. Native disclosure widgets, so it works without
 * JavaScript and every answer is in the page for search and screen readers.
 */
import { PATCHER_URL, REPOSITORY_URL } from "~/lib/content"
import { RELEASE_LABEL } from "~/lib/release"
---

<section aria-labelledby="faq" class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
  <p class="pixel-label text-logo-yellow">Questions</p>
  <h2 id="faq" class="pixel-heading mt-4">Before you set out</h2>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-3">
    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>How do I play it?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Wayfarer comes as a .ups patch. Apply it to your own Pokémon Emerald (U) ROM, for example
          with <a href={PATCHER_URL}>Rom Patcher JS</a> in your browser, and play the patched ROM in an
          emulator. The patch doesn't include the game itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>In an open world, won't I outlevel everything?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          No. Every badge, from any region, raises your level cap, and wild Pokémon, trainers and Poké Mart
          shelves grow with it. Early on, the grass off the road is dangerous. Later, routes become home
          ground and the Gym Leaders and leagues bring the real fights.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>Which emulators work?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Any up-to-date emulator that runs ROM hacks. These are known to work:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>PC and Mac:</strong> mGBA</li>
          <li><strong>Android:</strong> Pizza Boy, Lemuroid, or RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
          <li><strong>iOS:</strong> Delta, Ignited, or RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
          <li><strong>Linux handhelds:</strong> RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>How does it battle?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          With modern mechanics: the physical and special split, and updated stats, types and moves. TMs
          are reusable, so teach them as often as you like.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>Can I trade and battle with friends?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Trades and battles over the GBA link work, with a link cable or your emulator's link play.
          The GameCube, e-Reader and Berry Fix extras are gone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>Will my save carry over to updates?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>From v1.0 on, yes. Updates after that keep your save.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>Is it free?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Wayfarer is a free fan game, and you can follow every change
          <a href={REPOSITORY_URL}>on GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq pixel-corners pixel-panel" name="faq">
      <summary>When does it come out?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          On {RELEASE_LABEL}. <a href="/wayfarer-release.ics" download>Add it to your calendar</a>, or leave your
          email with Professor Oak and he'll write when it's out.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The game's menu cursor, pointing at the open answer. */
  .faq summary::after {
    content: "▶";
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--color-logo-yellow);
    transition: rotate 0.15s steps(2);
  }

  .faq[open] summary::after {
    rotate: 90deg;
  }

  .faq summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 4px solid var(--color-logo-yellow);
    outline-offset: -8px;
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: rgb(248 248 248 / 0.8);
  }

  .faq-answer ul {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: square;
  }

  .faq-answer strong {
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .faq-answer a {
    color: var(--color-logo-yellow);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .faq summary::after {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
